<p>The Trump administration has launched two sweeping trade investigations covering dozens of countries, a move that could clear the way for new tariffs after the US Supreme Court struck down much of President Trump’s earlier tariff program. US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer said the probes will look at concerns about excess industrial capacity (often framed as “overproduction”) and imports of goods made with forced labor, and he said he wants to wrap them up “as quickly as possible”. Major US trading partners are included. The overcapacity-focused probe names economies such as the European Union, China, Japan, India, Mexico, South Korea, Singapore, Switzerland, Taiwan and Vietnam. A separate forced-labor-focused investigation will examine whether countries’ policies do enough to combat forced labor, as part of a broader tariff approach the administration is developing. Overseas reactions mixed pushback with calls for clarity. China’s foreign ministry condemned the move as “political manipulation” and rejected the claim that overcapacity is a valid complaint. The European Commission said it would seek clarification on how a Section 301 investigation would interact with a recent EU-US tariff understanding, and warned it would respond “firmly and proportionately” to any breach of commitments.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/I9oYzH1i5r2gVD3tABMMJsUMM3J1Cekff3i0KE36p7VRrimj9LATqAoi5_9O28MyuRWdxhhexuuzQnoCNvI24QYLQSoEvsBEzeK2sg6FYeSi1cUVjHyxJfsQq0HCqp2HlJafsRXQ-5-ZI0KFCGbsPZNxcDt7ZR8QUWD_0bVWA1a63M9MBiZKOg' alt='Trucks leaving the Port of Los Angeles; the investigation is part of an effort to rebuild a tariff system after a Supreme Court ruling.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Diplomatic breadth: The Financial Times reported the new probes explicitly reach beyond US-China frictions to include close partners such as the UK, the EU and Canada, raising the risk of wider political fallout if tariffs follow.</li><li>China context: NPR reported Beijing cast the investigation as a “pretext” for tariffs as China pushed ahead with a new five-year economic plan that could further unsettle trade partners.</li><li>Two-track approach: US officials opened parallel Section 301 investigations—one focused on industrial “overproduction” and another on forced-labor-linked imports—creating separate records that could underpin different remedies.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer: Greer said the US is launching separate Section 301 probes—one on industrial overproduction and one on imports tied to forced labor—and that he wants to conclude them “as quickly as possible.” (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981535/us-launches-sweeping-trade-probe-against-dozens-of-nations'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>European Commission: The Commission said it would seek clarification on how the new probe would interact with last year’s EU-US tariff understanding and warned it would respond “firmly and proportionately” to any breach of commitments. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981535/us-launches-sweeping-trade-probe-against-dozens-of-nations'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Financial Times: The FT reported the probes name not only major economies but also close US allies including the UK, the EU and Canada, potentially widening the diplomatic impact of any follow-on tariff action. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/708a6a9a-3b93-4142-a923-de82450d4ab2'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>China’s foreign ministry (via NPR): China’s Foreign Ministry criticized the US investigation as a “pretext” for tariffs while China moved ahead with a five-year plan that could unsettle trade partners. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/12/nx-s1-5746061/us-china-trade-five-year-plan'>NPR</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/708a6a9a-3b93-4142-a923-de82450d4ab2'>US targets UK, EU and Canada in new round of tariff probes</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/12/us/politics/trump-forced-labor-tariffs.html'>Trump Targets Forced Labor in Global Tariff Scheme</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981535/us-launches-sweeping-trade-probe-against-dozens-of-nations'>US launches sweeping trade probe against dozens of nations</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/video-trump-administration-launches-unfair-trade-probes-in-bid-to-rebuild/'>Trump administration launches unfair-trade probes in bid to rebuild tariff pressure</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/12/nx-s1-5746061/us-china-trade-five-year-plan'>China slams Trump&#x27;s trade investigation, as it approves a 5-year economic plan</a> - npr.org</li></ul>